Statement of modification
-------------------------

1. The upstream Python implementation has been relocated, unmodified, to
   `original/`. It is retained as the parity reference that the Go port is
   tested against and as the source of the golden test vectors under
   `testdata/`. It is not built, published or installed by this repository.

2. The library has been reimplemented in Go. The Go code is an independent
   implementation written against the observable behaviour of the Python
   original; it reproduces that behaviour deliberately, including its edge
   cases, so that the two agree byte-for-byte on prompts and within 1e-4 on
   probabilities.

3. The Go port is inference only. The reinforcement-learning training math in
   the upstream package -- `proper_reward`, `td_lambda_targets` and
   `collate_items` -- has no Go counterpart and is not ported.

4. Several upstream inconsistencies are reproduced on purpose, because
   matching them is the point of a parity port, and several are deliberately
   not reproduced. Both sets are enumerated in `docs/INVARIANTS.md` and
   `PLAN.md`.

Code lifted from go-pocket-tts
------------------------------

The native backend's tensor runtime under `internal/runtime/` is lifted from:

    go-pocket-tts - pure-Go PocketTTS inference
    module github.com/cwbudde/go-pocket-tts
    commit fa68a5fc6cb02e0a9fc0fd62c573419b3ae0b449

go-pocket-tts is the copyright holder's own repository. It has no LICENSE
file, so this section is the record of where the code came from.

1. `internal/runtime/tensor` is lifted whole into `internal/runtime/tensor`:
   the tensor type, the shape and NN operations, the dot, axpy and GEMM
   kernels -- with Plan 9 assembly for dot and axpy on amd64 and for all
   three on arm64 -- the pure-Go fallbacks and the tests.

2. `internal/runtime/ops` is lifted into `internal/runtime/ops`: attention,
   MLP, RoPE, the kernel tolerance table and their tests and benchmarks.

3. Dropped: the 1-D convolutions -- `conv1d.go`, `convtranspose1d.go` and
   their tests; the `conv1d` and `convtranspose1d` tolerance entries and
   their keys in `TestKernelTolerance`; the conv benchmarks and
   `BenchmarkFrameDecodeThroughput`, which runs a transposed conv -- and,
   from `conv_runtime.go`, the conv worker setting (`SetConvWorkers`,
   `convWorkers`, `getConvWorkers`) and its test. `PERFORMANCE.md` is left
   out, because it is about the TTS model's kernels.

4. Modified: the import paths. `conv_runtime.go` is renamed `runtime.go`
   and keeps only the worker loop and scratch-buffer pool the attention
   kernels use; the pool's comment no longer names the conv paths. The
   test helper `randDataT` moves from `conv1d_test.go` to
   `test_helpers_test.go`. A package comment is added in `doc.go`. Lint
   fixes for this repository's configuration: `nolint` directives for
   `gocognit` on four kernels and for `cyclop` on two of them,
   `slices.Backward` in `computeStrides`, and an unused `nolint:funlen`
   removed from `Concat`.

